      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{600bb08cb76d6f78b108fb38|full_name}: The swivel sounds a bit different from what I'm proposing. It would still lock the player's lower body and restrict mouse movement to 90°, unless the player manually swivels the chair.\n... Which would also forcefully turn the player!\nThe canny you posted would also **almost** solve the issue! It wouldn't let us tether the player's position to the station, so it couldn't be used for vehicles.\nFor now I'm using teleports to work around all these issues, stations have too many restrictions >.<",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-13T13:40:29.450Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently stations with \"Immobilize\" lock the player's lower body in place, and prevent desktop using from rotating more than 90° to the left or right.\nThese restrictions make sense for cars, where the players are seated in a forward position.\nBut these restrictions prevent more advanced uses of stations. In several of my worlds I projects I would have liked to use stations, but couldn't.\nPlease give us an option to **not** lock the player's lower body in stations, and allow Desktop users to rotate more than 90°.",
